{"title":"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(kinda_bad)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (kinda bad)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The fraction \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/1/2e1249826c419acf9b5a00eb3f3f9acb191cc1d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac1{99^2}=0.\\overline{b_{n-1}b_{n-2}\\ldots b_2b_1b_0},\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the length of the period of the repeating decimal expansion.  What is the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f65fb8d86531d4ed6d4a522c85c51e62274f2972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_0+b_1+\\cdots+b_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89da78ebdeb8bc758e2bcd7137abe6ace4206e29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }874\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }883\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }887\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }891\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }892\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"443\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>the fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a741b33c2652e9b903f40a1420679d0dcdee06a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/4390881e118c5b4c8240b842b466517591116226.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum^{\\infty}_{n=1}\\dfrac{1}{10^{2n}}\\]\" width=\"64\" height=\"48\" />.\nsimilarly the fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/2/3b263e48248c123429879fb4d1a449ea8860f026.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{99^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"28\" height=\"37\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5e43af96acecd4b77ff2136c074a1b50781a701.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum^{\\infty}_{m=1}\\dfrac{1}{10^{2m}}\\sum^{\\infty}_{n=1}\\dfrac{1}{10^{2n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"140\" height=\"48\" /> which is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fa6acb4ddde579cb4a0ed9a8338a9aad195b09d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum^{\\infty}_{m=1}\\sum^{\\infty}_{n=1} \\dfrac{1}{10^{2(m+n)}}\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"48\" />\nand we can see that for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4323b5dd841ea9ef2dca82e10cbc9deef9b326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+m=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/b/79b1612f577754eb38a3a61b200883fce9f03a1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n,m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> combinations so the above sum is equivalent to:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06db84aab337411b42a9811c3454520c711583f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum^{\\infty}_{k=2}\\dfrac{k-1}{10^{2k}}\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"48\" />\nwe note that the sequence starts repeating at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e2268394d59ffa8259b6e03efa10ad21133a6355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 102$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />\nyet consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/90065a67f95644855ef2b955fc89a6e91107e38e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum^{101}_{k=99}\\dfrac{k-1}{10^{2k}}=\\dfrac{98}{{10^{198}}}+\\dfrac{99}{{10^{200}}}+\\dfrac{100}{10^{{202}}}=\\dfrac{1}{10^{198}}(98+\\dfrac{99}{100}+\\dfrac{100}{10000})=\\dfrac{1}{10^{198}}(98+\\dfrac{99}{100}+\\dfrac{1}{100})=\\dfrac{1}{10^{198}}(98+\\dfrac{100}{100})=\\dfrac{1}{10^{198}}(99)\\]\" width=\"900\" height=\"50\" />\nso the decimal will go from 1 to 99 skipping the number 98\nand we can easily compute the sum of the digits from 0 to 99 to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab8befb03ae1a73d638ebde336a7967cd10c8f82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[45\\cdot10\\cdot2=900\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"13\" /> subtracting the sum of the digits of 98 which is 17 we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f865fdf8ef47666208820fda82567e614f0df96.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[900-17=883\\textbf{(B) }\\qquad\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/f/b9f4ef18b27722e1e14a56f715893d8d00beaf25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{99^2}\\\\\\\\ =\\frac{1}{99} \\cdot \\frac{1}{99}\\\\\\\\ =\\frac{0.\\overline{01}}{99}\\\\\\\\ =0.\\overline{00010203...9799}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"157\" height=\"159\" />\n</p><p>So, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/9/9c935af325194e48f0bf7760edd02b01409ea10c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0+0+0+1+0+2+0+3+...+9+7+9+9=2\\cdot10\\cdot\\frac{9\\cdot10}{2}-(9+8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"588\" height=\"37\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748f63c1d6644030089d4c983f994e5c00a002aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 883}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"73\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>There are two things to notice here. First, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70444365e2b2f1ff8ab870e7c64ea5311d86f5f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> has a very simple and unique decimal expansion, as shown. Second, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/8/0e81a2270c43eb1c6a437e2bb00bb813e106854b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{0.\\overline{01}}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"34\" height=\"39\" /> to itself produce a repeating decimal, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> has to evenly divide a sufficiently extended number of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdcf7c34633dc11d3bef08bbedb12352d21319bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101010101..$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />. This number will have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ones (197 digits in total), as to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The enormity of this number forces us to look for a pattern, and so we divide out as shown. Indeed, upon division (seeing how the remainders always end in \"501\" or \"601\" or, at last, \"9801\"), we find the repeating part <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e16108d2dbaf3391934a94d31b4bbd889f4ed09b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.00010203040506070809101112131415....9799$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"351\" height=\"13\" />. If we wanted to further check our pattern, we could count the total number of digits in our quotient (not counting the first three): 195. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac002e358da97f56413b26f1eee415c827fa6b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99&lt;100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />, multiplying by it will produce either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> extra digits, so our quotient passes the test.\n</p><p>Or note that the 1 has to be carried when you get to 100 so the 99 becomes 00 and the 1 gets carried again to 98 which becomes 99. \n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28kinda_bad.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(kinda_bad)\">Solution 3 (kinda bad)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (kinda bad)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a66494300362939f9fba4a50125add9841a7e6c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[99^2=9801\\]\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" /> Does 9801 look familiar? The fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c162da52a57f3608f82571bd6f67ebf49c7529e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{9801}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"38\" /> is a very famous fraction, because when expressed as a decimal, it equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/8319263e9332aee777a887dac4830da20aaa0cdb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0.0001020304050607080910...9091929394959697990001020304...\\]\" width=\"496\" height=\"13\" /> (the numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/b/04bb0118c67774bf78771e91eb8ad476da5654b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$00-99 \\textbf{ EXCEPT } 98$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"170\" height=\"15\" />). You should look at the above solutions for the reason. The sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/73119f04d6ae5f6eb4afc8c9c946a5744a11be50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so therefore, adding 17 to all of the choices should be a nice number. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e226c2f5a445f0a9ab589c1337336ea7587b36e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/c/46cda75a5fcaf091c43adad52f02e3d9f596d5ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$883+17=900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />, which is very nice, so our answer should be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748f63c1d6644030089d4c983f994e5c00a002aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 883}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"73\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Namish Dour\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2014amc12a/382\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2014amc12a/382</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A\">2014 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017233806\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.071 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 303/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7898/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.219      1 -total\n 58.96%    8.973      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 38.14%    5.804      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12360:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017233806 and revision id 290377. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}